course: dictionary
lesson: 13650
title: A word for too many pests
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An infestation is a large number of insects, animals or pests living in a place where they are not wanted and causing harm. Look at the clues in the sentence: a large number, a place they should not be, and harm. «The kitchen had an infestation of ants after the spilt jam.» Ants in the kitchen are not wanted, and there are many of them.
explain: Ask what the word is doing in the sentence. «The school sent a letter home about a head lice infestation.» The letter is about something bad that lots of lice are causing. Infestation is the big problem, and head lice are the pests in it.
explain: Try swapping in your own meaning. «The rose bush had an infestation of aphids.» Replace infestation with a large number of pests living where they are not wanted: "The rose bush had a large number of pests living where they are not wanted of aphids." It does not read smoothly, but the idea fits: the aphids are many, and they are harming the rose.
fact: An infestation is a large number of pests, not just one or two.
fact: Insects, animals and pests can all cause an infestation: head lice, mice, ants, moths and aphids are examples.
fact: «Infestation» is a noun, so you can say an infestation, or more than one infestation.
fact: Pest control is the work of dealing with pests, such as mice or ants, when they become an infestation.
fact: An infestation is always a problem, because the pests are not wanted and they cause harm.
exercise: «The kitchen had an infestation of ants after the spilt jam.» What does infestation mean? | A special kind of kitchen cupboard | A short summer holiday | A tasty jam recipe | *A large number of pests living where they are not wanted
exercise: «The school sent a letter home about a head lice infestation.» Why did the school send the letter? | To say the school will be closed for a holiday | *To warn parents about lots of head lice causing harm | To tell parents about a new sports day | To ask for money for a school trip
exercise: «Hundreds of aphids covered the rose bush.» Find and copy the word that shows there were a very large number. | rose | bush | *Hundreds | aphids
test: «The mice had an infestation in the old barn.» What is an infestation? | A pile of hay | A barn with fresh paint | A kind of farm animal | *Too many pests living somewhere they are not wanted
test: A company is called in for pest control at the school. What is its job? | To grow more pests | *To deal with pests that are causing harm | To feed the school animals | To paint the classroom walls
exam: Which word means a large number of pests living where they are not wanted and causing harm? | Festival | Vacation | *Infestation | Harvest
